HTTP Versions :-
Now we will study about the different versions of HTTP -

* HTTP/1.0 -> One TCP connection over request/responst pair.
* HTTP/1.1 -> Reusing a single TCP connection for multiple sequential request.
* HTTP/2 -> It lets your browser send and recieve many requests at once over a single connection.
* HTTP/3 -> Uses QUIC over UDP, improving connection establishment and handling packet loss differently from TCP-based HTTP/2

